  "body": "**Google Calendar and speed tiers**\n\n### Highlights\n\n- Google login lets you pick which services to connect and adds a built-in calendar tool for viewing, creating, updating, and deleting events\n- Guided Google OAuth app setup that detects existing gcloud credentials, validates generated project IDs, and imports the app automatically\n- Alt+Up/Down cycles the speed tier between Standard, Fast, and Ultrafast\n- New /desktop command opens the current session in Jcode Desktop\n\n### Improvements\n\n- MCP tool results and mcp_search output are fitted to token budgets instead of fixed caps, and accept_large_output returns the full result\n- The mcp list action lists only tool names, and mcp_search ranks name matches first\n- Todo quality gates share rows instead of taking one line each\n\n### Fixes\n\n- Browser actions target the right browser when several run the bridge extension\n- Interrupting a coordinator stops the swarm workers it spawned (thanks @SiavZ)\n- A per-call swarm spawn_mode of auto defers to your configured mode (thanks @SiavZ)\n- /restart and /reload from a remote client no longer wipe the server's transcript (thanks @SiavZ)\n- The shared server reloads after an install repoints the link it started from (thanks @SiavZ)\n- run --json and --ndjson report the local or direct profile instead of openrouter\n- Fixed swarm plan and status handlers that could stall the server\n\n**Full changelog**: https://github.com/1jehuang/jcode/compare/v0.90.1...v0.91.0\n\n<!-- jcode-platform-availability:start -->\n## Platform availability\n\n- Linux x86_64: available\n- Linux aarch64: available\n- macOS Apple Silicon: available\n- macOS Intel: available\n- Windows x86_64: available\n- Windows ARM64: available\n- FreeBSD x86_64: available\n<!-- jcode-platform-availability:end -->\n\n<!-- jcode-discord-announced:v0.91.0 -->\n",
